From: razgulay <bantran09@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:21:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] fix(vertex): terminal-user gate on the final wire body
 + 400 payload dump
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After the role fix, Vertex moved to the next rejection: 'Requests ending
with a model turn are not supported.' The translator's terminal-turn
guard provably fires for every shape probed (assistant-last, tool flows,
multi-round), so the shape must resurface between the translator and the
socket. ForwardVertex now re-establishes the guarantee on the final wire
body — EnsureGeminiTerminalUserTurn appends the guard turn (a
functionResponse per unanswered call, else a Continue. nudge) when the
contents end with model, map-based so unknown top-level fields survive.
It runs BEFORE the vertex post-process so the synthesized guard ids get
the vertex id strip.

Every vertex 400 also dumps its exact request body to
/tmp/9router-vertex-400.json (same post-mortem pattern as
ForwardGemini), so the next schema rejection is diagnosable against the
payload that drew it instead of guesswork.
---
